00:47:38.280 --> 00:47:39.900
Someone has a question
about-- suppose

00:47:39.900 --> 00:47:43.517
I want to modify the
generated HTML file and keep

00:47:43.517 --> 00:47:44.850
these changes when I knit later.

00:47:44.850 --> 00:47:47.430
Is it possible to do so?

00:47:47.430 --> 00:47:48.540
Not really.

00:47:48.540 --> 00:47:52.950
I think my general answer is,
all of the output directories

00:47:52.950 --> 00:47:54.600
that we showed you here today--

00:47:54.600 --> 00:47:56.310
every time you
rebuild your site,

00:47:56.310 --> 00:47:58.350
they're going to get
overwritten every time.

00:47:58.350 --> 00:48:01.680
So if you wanted to have
some HTML that you wanted

00:48:01.680 --> 00:48:03.600
to carry through,
you can actually

00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:07.500
use raw HTML in your
Rmd source files

00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:11.280
and have them translate into
the generated HTML file.

00:48:11.280 --> 00:48:13.470
But in general, I
wouldn't recommend

00:48:13.470 --> 00:48:15.990
editing any of the output
directories that we showed.

00:48:15.990 --> 00:48:17.730
So for an R Markdown
or an Distill site,

00:48:17.730 --> 00:48:21.330
that _site folder,
bookdown, that _book folder,

00:48:21.330 --> 00:48:24.110
and for blogdown, it
was the _public folder--

00:48:24.110 --> 00:48:27.180
I would never recommend editing
by hand any of those files,

00:48:27.180 --> 00:48:29.250
because anytime you want
to update your content,

00:48:29.250 --> 00:48:32.050
those are going to
get rewritten for you.

00:48:32.050 --> 00:48:34.900
Is that accurate according to
what you think, Desiree, also?

00:48:34.900 --> 00:48:36.067
DESIREE DE LEON: Absolutely.

00:48:36.067 --> 00:48:38.230
Yeah, don't touch
anything in those folders,

00:48:38.230 --> 00:48:40.240
because it will mostly
be a waste of your time.

00:48:40.240 --> 00:48:44.550
As soon as you knit,
it will all wash away.

00:48:44.550 --> 00:48:49.210
But yeah, putting raw HTML into
the R Markdown file itself--

00:48:49.210 --> 00:48:52.410
that works just great, and
actually I do that a lot.

00:48:56.611 --> 00:48:59.130
ALISON HILL: Let's see.

