Sometimes I deploy
sites via Netlify.

00:50:11.100 --> 00:50:13.570
sometimes I use GitHub pages.

00:50:13.570 --> 00:50:18.510
It largely depends for me on the
kind of project I'm working on

00:50:18.510 --> 00:50:22.950
and what kind of link I want
to be able to link out to

00:50:22.950 --> 00:50:24.240
and how much I'm updating it.

00:50:24.240 --> 00:50:26.820
So I tend to defer
to Netlify, mostly

00:50:26.820 --> 00:50:28.320
because I have a
lot of sites there,

00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:30.450
and it's a nicer
interface for me and.

00:50:30.450 --> 00:50:32.190
The majority of my
sites are blogdown,

00:50:32.190 --> 00:50:35.370
and blogdown has a
nice feature, or Hugo

00:50:35.370 --> 00:50:37.170
has a nice feature
that's actually,

00:50:37.170 --> 00:50:39.460
Netlify can build
Hugo sites for you.

00:50:39.460 --> 00:50:43.400
So when you serve your
site locally in RStudio,

00:50:43.400 --> 00:50:45.900
what you're essentially doing
is knitting all of your source

00:50:45.900 --> 00:50:49.035
files into HTML
or Markdown files,

00:50:49.035 --> 00:50:50.910
and then Netlify can
build your site for you.

00:50:50.910 --> 00:50:52.952
So it's nice, because I'm
able to outsource that,

00:50:52.952 --> 00:50:57.300
and that also allows me
to be able to use GitHub

00:50:57.300 --> 00:51:00.400
throughout my workflow a little
bit easier with blogdown.

00:51:00.400 --> 00:51:03.310
But with the other options,
I think I go back and forth.

00:51:03.310 --> 00:51:05.760
I do tend to use
Netlify more, but I

00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:09.815
wouldn't say it's a
completely strong preference.

00:51:09.815 --> 00:51:11.190
So Desiree, you
seem like you can

00:51:11.190 --> 00:51:12.510
see more questions than I can.

00:51:12.510 --> 00:51:13.660
DESIREE DE LEON: Yeah, I
think I must be able to--

00:51:13.890 --> 00:51:14.190
ALISON HILL: If you want
to read out any other ones,

00:51:14.190 --> 00:51:15.370
I only see three.

00:51:15.370 --> 00:51:19.070
DESIREE DE LEON: OK,
here's another question.

00:51:19.070 --> 00:51:23.520
I created index.Rmd, but the
tab Build Site does not appear.

00:51:23.520 --> 00:51:24.990
What d I have to do?

00:51:24.990 --> 00:51:27.720
ALISON HILL: Restart RStudio.

00:51:27.720 --> 00:51:31.570
So sometimes it might not yet
detect all the files in there

00:51:31.570 --> 00:51:35.760
for it to identify that it needs
to show you that Build Book

00:51:35.760 --> 00:51:37.020
or Build Site button.

00:51:37.020 --> 00:51:39.600
So restart RStudio, open
that R project file again,

00:51:39.600 --> 00:51:43.225
and you should
see that populate.

00:51:43.225 --> 00:51:44.350
DESIREE DE LEON: OK, great.

00:51:49.867 --> 00:51:52.450
Why does signing up to Netlify
using a version control account

00:51:52.450 --> 00:51:53.680
make your life easier?

00:51:53.680 --> 00:51:55.540
ALISON HILL: It makes
your life easier

00:51:55.540 --> 00:51:57.070
if you use GitHub already.

00:51:57.070 --> 00:51:58.840
If you don't use
GitHub already, then it

00:51:58.840 --> 00:52:00.940
may not make much of
a difference to you.

00:52:00.940 --> 00:52:03.760
But the reason why I
say that is because you

00:52:03.760 --> 00:52:06.670
can keep your files that
are already in GitHub

00:52:06.670 --> 00:52:08.530
and have Netlify
connect to those.

00:52:08.530 --> 00:52:11.170
So whenever you make
a change locally

00:52:11.170 --> 00:52:13.390
on your computer
to your website,

00:52:13.390 --> 00:52:16.612
you build your site
locally, you can see it.

00:52:16.612 --> 00:52:18.070
You push to GitHub,
and then that's

00:52:18.070 --> 00:52:19.840
all you have to
remember to do is,

00:52:19.840 --> 00:52:21.910
you just have to push
it to, GitHub and you

00:52:21.910 --> 00:52:24.950
don't have to do any extra step
to actually deploy or publish

00:52:24.950 --> 00:52:25.450
your site.

00:52:25.450 --> 00:52:27.790
So the way we showed you
today in this webinar

00:52:27.790 --> 00:52:29.320
was a very manual way.

00:52:29.320 --> 00:52:31.510
It's not a bad way, but
it's a very manual way

00:52:31.510 --> 00:52:34.060
of dragging and dropping
physically that folder

00:52:34.060 --> 00:52:37.420
into Netlify, to both
deploy it the first time

00:52:37.420 --> 00:52:38.892
and to update it.

00:52:38.892 --> 00:52:40.600
And so that could wear
on you after a bit

00:52:40.600 --> 00:52:41.920
if you're updating frequently.

00:52:41.920 --> 00:52:43.753
If you have a site
that's just kind of done,

00:52:43.753 --> 00:52:46.310
and you want to share it, then
that's not really a big deal.

00:52:46.310 --> 00:52:48.190
But if you're updating
and maybe adding

00:52:48.190 --> 00:52:51.370
materials every couple
days or every week,

00:52:51.370 --> 00:52:52.870
you may want to
think about starting

00:52:52.870 --> 00:52:54.790
to use version control.

00:52:54.790 --> 00:52:56.590
But we didn't want
to necessarily depend

00:52:56.590 --> 00:52:58.965
on that for this workshop,
because we wanted to make sure

00:52:58.965 --> 00:53:02.140
that we optimized for being able
to share on short notice, which

00:53:02.140 --> 00:53:04.036
for me does not involve GitHub.

00:53:04.036 --> 00:53:06.370
[LAUGHS]

00:53:06.370 --> 00:53:07.960
DESIREE DE LEON: Agreed.

00:53:07.960 --> 00:53:09.350
OK, here's another question.

00:53:09.350 --> 00:53:11.225
I actually don't know
the answer to this one.

00:53:11.225 --> 00:53:12.880
It is, what if I
would prefer not

00:53:12.880 --> 00:53:16.373
to use Netlify but a university
server to store my material?

00:53:16.373 --> 00:53:17.290
ALISON HILL: Oh, yeah.

00:53:17.290 --> 00:53:18.340
You can do that as well.

00:53:18.340 --> 00:53:20.225
I did that [INAUDIBLE].

00:53:20.225 --> 00:53:22.600
All you really need to know
is know the output directory,

00:53:22.600 --> 00:53:23.225
right, Desiree?

00:53:23.225 --> 00:53:26.050
As long as you can drag and drop
or place that somewhere, then

00:53:26.050 --> 00:53:27.280
you've got a hosted website.

00:53:29.715 --> 00:53:31.090
DESIREE DE LEON:
Yeah, as soon as

00:53:31.090 --> 00:53:34.630
you have those HTML
files in some place,

00:53:34.630 --> 00:53:36.510
then you can use
whatever server you want,

00:53:36.510 --> 00:53:40.957
following the instructions
of whatever that server uses.

00:53:40.957 --> 00:53:42.790
ALISON HILL: But that's
why it's really nice

00:53:42.790 --> 00:53:47.590
to know where the site actually
is, because your source

00:53:47.590 --> 00:53:49.720
files are in your project
folder, but knowing where

00:53:49.720 --> 00:53:52.925
the actual website lives
and the directory is nice,

00:53:52.925 --> 00:53:54.550
because that's the
only folder that you

00:53:54.550 --> 00:53:59.110
need to be able to share.

00:53:59.110 --> 00:54:00.370
